            <ArticleTitle>The use of laparoscopy in the management of right iliac fossa pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>68-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Fourty-six patients with a clinical diagnosis of acute appendicitis were laparoscoped before exploration. As a result the diagnosis was revised in 10 patients (22%). With experience the laparoscopic features of appendicitis can be recognised confidently so reducing the number of normal appendices removed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
